            <ArticleTitle>[Analysis of lung function in children with respiratory diseases and its clinical application].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>365-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To evaluate the clinical application of lung function analysis in diagnosis of children respiratory diseases.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Respiratory function was evaluated with portable lung function detector in 6 261 children with respiratory diseases. FEV1, FVC and PEFR were measured in 268 children with cough variant asthma (CVA) and 147 children with asthma (AS), and the results were self-compared during follow-up.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULT" NlmCategory="RESULTS">There were no significant differences in above parameters between children with cough variant asthma and those with asthma (P&gt;0.05). Lung functions of asthma children were improved evidently by administration of glycocorticoid inhalator (P&lt;0.001).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Lung function detection is essential for diagnosis of asthma and it can be used as a reliable index for therapeutic effect of asthma children.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
